Falsifies `address_space_map::verification::service_window_refuses_every_address_its_doc_forbids`.

The defect: `service_window` treats its band as closed at the top, so the first page of the image
band, `0x6000_0000`, is returned as a service window.

Expected to fail: the harness reaches `refused_inputs_never_reach_here` (an unwinding failure, not a
panic), so Kani reports "encountered failures other than panics".

diff --git a/crates/address_space_map/src/lib.rs b/crates/address_space_map/src/lib.rs
index 0eba0def7..7c4b745cf 100644
--- a/crates/address_space_map/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/address_space_map/src/lib.rs
@@ -181,7 +181,7 @@ pub const fn service_window(va: u64) -> u64 {
         "a service window must be page aligned"
     );
     assert!(
-        SERVICE_WINDOWS.contains(va),
+        SERVICE_WINDOWS.contains(va) || va == SERVICE_WINDOWS.end,
         "a service window must lie in SERVICE_WINDOWS (address_space_map)"
     );
     va
